Task: Wire Redis-backed CartStore into Main, docker-compose, config (Phase 3, final, of redis-cart-model_20261002)

Summary: Wired the standalone RedisConfig(uri, ttlSeconds) from Phase 2 into the
aggregate CartServiceConfig as a required `redis` field; added application.conf's
redis block (uri defaults to redis://localhost:6379, ttl defaults to 86400s/24h, both
env-overridable via REDIS_URI/CART_TTL_SECONDS, mirroring order-service's own
pattern). Replaced docker-compose.yml's postgres service entirely with a redis:7-
alpine service (redis-cli ping healthcheck) - no volume, since cart data is
deliberately ephemeral. Updated Main.scala to build/use CartStore.redis(config.redis,
meter, logger) in place of the temporary CartStore.inMemory introduced in Phase 1.
HealthRoutesSuite/CartDocsSuite's stub stores needed no changes - their trait shape
was already correct from Phase 1, the plan's own wording anticipated a need that
turned out already satisfied.

Verified sbt coverage test coverageReport: 90.28% statement / 90.00% branch - well
above the >80% target, no new tests needed to close a gap.

Files modified:
- src/main/scala/cartservice/CartServiceConfig.scala (redis field added to the
  aggregate config)
- src/main/resources/application.conf (redis block added)
- docker-compose.yml (postgres -> redis)
- src/main/scala/cartservice/Main.scala (CartStore.redis wired in)
- src/test/scala/cartservice/CartServiceConfigSuite.scala (redis fixtures added)

Why: closes out redis-cart-model_20261002 - cart-service now runs against Redis
only, with no Postgres anywhere in the repo, matching
gluon/docs/system-design.md's "Redis only, primary store" row for this service.

